<!-- Fissure's fallen rocks (Spec v2, 2026-07-22). The v1 fifteen from design/fissure-rock-list.md.
     Thrown channels ride native parts (grenades, BleedingOnHit, DischargeOnHit); step channels and
     pathfinding asymmetry rode Cleo_TerraFirma_FallenRockPart, in quarantine/ since 2026-09-30. Crush-on-landing is read from the
     Cleo_TerraFirma_CrushDamage / Cleo_TerraFirma_CrushInstakill tags by the mutation.

     GRIND-FIRST (RULED 2026-07-22): rocks are NOT direct cooking ingredients; the pantry opens
     only through the mill (pestle anywhere, campfire menu, or a millstone). All rock-side
     PreparedCookingIngredient lines were removed that day; the cooking domains live on the
     Ground_* forms at the bottom of this file. The per-rock "Lithovore pass" comments below
     describe each rock's DOMAIN ASSIGNMENT, which its ground form carries. Eaten-effect tags and
     parts (the raw channel) remain rock-side and are unaffected. -->
<objects>
	<!-- BETA HOLD (user ruling 2026-07-27): every spawnable's Description below is commented out
	     (BETA-HELD markers) so unapproved draft text does not ship in the friends beta; rocks fall
	     back to their inherited base-game description. Restore at the real text pass. -->
	<!-- shared base: a throwable stone that fell from the ceiling -->
	<!-- V1 ROCK CATALOG + KITCHEN PARKED on branch quarantine-hold (2026-08-22, user ruling:
	     "move it to its own branch so it doesn't come up until i'm ready to address it").
	     This file keeps the live fissure spine (base fallen rock, pebbles, rubble,
	     crumbled wall, fabric wall) The redoubt figure and crack joined them 2026-09-30.
	     The chasm, ape statue and baboon figurine + fists moved to quarantine/ 2026-09-30. Generic debris left the spine 2026-08-25 (user: base rocks). The payload stones, puddles, tar patch, ground/kitchen forms,
	     StoneMeal, cooking ingredient mappings, surge field and force shards live on that branch;
	     design record in TODO-quarantine.md. -->
	<object Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_BaseFallenRock" Inherits="BaseStone">
		<!-- Weight 5 -> 1 (user ruling 2026-07-22 verification session): fissure stones are light;
		     a pocketful of ammo shouldn't be half a carry budget. Stalactite overrides back to 5
		     (ruled); pebbles override to 0. KNOWN KNOCK-ON, flagged for veto: the Lithovore's
		     size-scaled satiety keys off weight <= 1, so all fissure rocks now eat as HALF snacks
		     (was: full). Stalactite/boulders/statues unchanged. -->
		<part Name="Physics" Weight="1" Category="Thrown Weapons" />
		<part Name="Commerce" Value="1" />
		<!-- Cleo_TerraFirma_FallenRockPart (step payloads, pathfinding asymmetry, the discharge law)
		     moved to quarantine/ 2026-09-30: no live stone used any of it. -->
		<tag Name="BaseObject" Value="*noinherit" />
		<tag Name="ExcludeFromDynamicEncounters" />
		<tag Name="Tier" Value="1" />
	</object>

	<!-- ============ Band 1 (mutation Lv 1-3) ============ -->


	<object Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_Rock_Pebbles" Inherits="Cleo_TerraFirma_BaseFallenRock">
		<part Name="Render" DisplayName="pebbles" Tile="Items/sw_smallstone.bmp" ColorString="&amp;w" DetailColor="Y" />
		<part Name="Description" Short="Smooth spall from the world's slow grinding, come down at last." /> <!-- draft, approved 2026-09-30 -->
		<part Name="Physics" Weight="0" /> <!-- user asked 0.1; engine Weight is an int, so 0 is the nearest (powder precedent) -->
		<tag Name="Gender" Value="plural" />
		<tag Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_CrushDamage" Value="1" />
	</object>
	<!-- (russet/blue pebble variants CUT, user ruling 2026-07-22) -->

	<!-- (russet/blue pebble variants CUT, user ruling 2026-07-22) -->

	<!-- (Rock_Generic "fallen rock" DELETED, user ruling 2026-08-25 "remove em":
	     base rocks serve everywhere it spawned. Dress: Small Stone/SmallBoulder;
	     fissure debris: SmallBoulder. Its 2d6 CrushDamage left with it.) -->

	<!-- THE HOLOGRAPHIC ROCK (user concept 2026-07-24, designed + ruled 2026-07-25): the rock
	     that isn't there. Belief gates both ends (Part_Holographic: Int DC 12, sticky forever,
	     machines auto-pass); a believed hit does EXACTLY a generic rock's dice (the mundanity is
	     the punchline) and collapses the lie. Generics of tiers 2-3 at weight 5 ("it's just a
	     joke rock, so it's pretty weak... it should also not get picked for seams"); NoSeam tag
	     enforced at the Fissure seam roll. No CrushDamage tag: a fall that isn't there crushes
	     no one. Excluded from the strange pool (purity invariant: a belief gate can no-op).
	     Neither mill nor pestle yields anything (machines don't believe; believers grind at
	     nothing). Render shimmer = HologramMaterial, the tell for the observant. Name WIP,
	     queued behind the tanglelith slate; description DRAFT (user's surface). -->

	<object Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_Rock_Rubble" Inherits="Rubble">
		<part Name="Render" DisplayName="rubble" ColorString="&amp;y" DetailColor="w" />
		<!-- BETA-HELD: <part Name="Description" Short="A volume of the ceiling lies where it landed, broken past any use but blocking the way all the same." /> -->
		<stat Name="Hitpoints" Value="250" />
		<tag Name="ExcludeFromDynamicEncounters" />
		<tag Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_CrushDamage" Value="3d6" />
	</object>

	<!-- ============ Rock-scale puddles (pool-volume ruling 2026-07-24; revised same day from
	     2d8 to 4d8, so 4-32 drams) ============
	     The base puddles spawn at a flat 500 drams and render as "pool of X" (a water source
	     from a pebble); base OilPuddle's own StartVolume idiom is the fix pattern. These children
	     override spawn volume only; everything else inherits. The pour-into-container park item
	     draws from the same 2d8 budget. -->

	<object Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_Rock_CrumbledWall" Inherits="Rubble">
		<part Name="Render" DisplayName="crumbled wall" ColorString="&amp;Y" DetailColor="y" />
		<!-- BETA-HELD: <part Name="Description" Short="A slab too broken to stand and too stubborn to lie flat." /> -->
		<stat Name="Hitpoints" Value="400" />
		<tag Name="ExcludeFromDynamicEncounters" />
		<tag Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_CrushDamage" Value="5d6" />
	</object>


	<object Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_Rock_Wall" Inherits="Sandstone">
		<part Name="Render" DisplayName="fallen wall" />
		<!-- BETA-HELD: <part Name="Description" Short="A shelf of the deep ceiling, standing now where it fell, load-bearing for nothing." /> -->
		<tag Name="ExcludeFromDynamicEncounters" />
		<tag Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_CrushDamage" Value="8d8" />
		<tag Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_CrushInstakill" Value="15" />
		<!-- seam fix (user 2026-08-05: "fissure walls don't seem to paint with calcify walls"):
		     the painter only fuses same-blueprint / matching-PaintWith / neighbor-wildcard /
		     PaintPart-hit neighbors, and this blueprint matched calcify's zone-borrowed stone on
		     none of them. PaintPart makes THIS wall draw fused toward anything carrying the mod's
		     stone part (calcify walls, zone geology; Merges.xml puts it on all natural rock);
		     PaintWith "*" is the engine wildcard making neighbors draw fused toward THIS wall.
		     Both directions covered = no broken faces at the joint. -->
		<tag Name="PaintWith" Value="*" />
		<tag Name="PaintPart" Value="Cleo_TerraFirma_StoneshaperWallProperties" />
	</object>


</objects>
